                <pb facs="0238" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg176"/>

                <head>No. 120.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitt to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="received-date" when="1878-06-13">June 13,
                    1878</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris.</hi></placeName>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evarts</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Secretary, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Learn at foreign office France consulted members Latin Union, intimating
                    inclination to accept, but not alone.</p>
                <p>Belgium accepted, first suggesting preliminary conference of Union. Switzerland
                    approved this. France thought this unnecessary. Union should await American
                    propositions, and then consult. Italy agreed and accepted, naming October.
                    France replied American law limited six months. France now suggests United
                    States propose date for conference. Intimates that end June, or early July would
                    be acceptable.</p>
                <closer><signed>HITT, <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
